<BaseLayout title="Warning symbols and messages">
  <h1>Warning symbols and messages</h1>
  <p>The symbol is only part of the information. Read and record the accompanying driver-display message; the same general warning symbol may appear with different messages and required actions.</p>

  <h2>Red warnings — treat as urgent</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Warning</th><th>Meaning / response</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>General red warning</th><td>A fault may affect safety or drivability. Read the message and follow its instruction; stop if directed.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Low oil pressure</th><td>Stop the engine immediately. Check oil level when safe. If level is normal or warning remains, contact a workshop.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>High engine temperature</th><td>Stop safely and follow the display instruction. Never open the cooling system while hot.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Brake system fault</th><td>Read the message and seek service. Stop if braking performance is abnormal or the display directs you to stop.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Airbag / SRS</th><td>A safety-system fault has been detected. Arrange workshop diagnosis; do not work on airbag circuits yourself.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Electrical system fault</th><td>Read the message and arrange workshop diagnosis, especially if starting, steering, braking, or other vehicle functions are affected.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Amber warnings</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Warning</th><th>Meaning / response</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Information symbol</th><td>A vehicle system has a problem. Read the driver-display message.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>ABS fault</th><td>ABS may be unavailable while conventional braking remains. Drive cautiously only if the vehicle brakes normally and the manual permits; arrange diagnosis.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Emission-control fault</th><td>Have the vehicle checked. If the engine runs roughly, loses power, overheats, or the warning flashes, stop and seek assistance.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Tire-pressure system</th><td>Check all tires promptly using the door-placard cold pressures. A flashing-then-steady warning can indicate a system fault rather than low pressure alone.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Stability system</th><td>A steady warning may indicate a fault; a flashing symbol can indicate system intervention. Read the message.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Do not rely on color alone</h2>
  <p>Some indicators simply show that a feature is active. For example, turn signals and high beams have normal status indicators. Use the symbol description in the correct model-year manual rather than a generic dashboard-symbol chart.</p>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.volvocars.com/us/support/car/s60/20w46">Volvo Cars — 2021 S60 owner's information</a>. See Displays and voice control → Indicator and warning symbols. The exact market-specific manual and the message shown in the vehicle take precedence.</p>
</BaseLayout>
